---
name: lossless-memory
description: Recall details from persisted Pi sessions with Lossless Claw tools.
---

# Lossless Memory

Use these tools when details from persisted Pi sessions matter.

1. Call `lcm_sessions` to orient by recent session header IDs and paths.
2. Call `lcm_grep` with distinctive terms, an optional session ID, and narrow role or time filters.
3. Call `lcm_expand_query` to recover bounded neighboring evidence around promising matches.
4. Call `lcm_describe` to inspect one session's active leaf, branch shape, and retained summaries.

Prefer exact file names, command names, error text, and user terminology. Treat Pi session JSONL,
compaction entries, and branches as authoritative. Cite the returned session header ID and path
when recovered context affects an answer.
